<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Feedback to resources - AI Gene Review</title>
    {% include "_site_style.html.j2" %}
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
    <div class="panel">
        <div class="crumbs"><a href="../../index.html">AI Gene Review</a></div>
        <h1>Feedback to resources</h1>
        <p class="muted">What the reviews here send back to other resources: changes to ontologies,
            corrections to annotation records, verdicts on vocabulary-to-GO mappings, and reviews of
            annotation rules. Reports and TSVs are generated from the review files at each site build.</p>
        <div class="stats">
            <div><strong>{{ ontologies | sum(attribute="total") }}</strong>ontology changes</div>
            <div><strong>{{ terms }}</strong>proposed new terms</div>
            <div><strong>{{ open_defects }}</strong>open source defects</div>
            <div><strong>{{ mapping_projects | length }}</strong>mapping reviews</div>
            <div><strong>{{ rule_reviews }}</strong>rule reviews</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" id="ontology-changes">
        <h2>Ontology changes</h2>
        <p class="muted">Structured <code>proposed_ontology_changes</code> on gene reviews, modules and
            project pages. <em>Requests</em> are changes asked of the ontology; the <em>inbound</em>
            worklist is upstream changes our own content still has to adopt.
            <a href="ontology-changes.tsv">Download TSV</a>.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
            <thead><tr><th>Ontology</th><th class="num">Changes</th><th class="num">Open requests</th><th class="num">Inbound to adopt</th><th>Reports</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
            {% for o in ontologies %}
            <tr><td>{{ o.ontology }}</td><td class="num">{{ o.total }}</td><td class="num">{{ o.outbound }}</td><td class="num">{{ o.inbound }}</td>
                <td><a href="ontology-changes/{{ o.ontology }}-requests.html">requests</a> &middot;
                    <a href="ontology-changes/{{ o.ontology }}-inbound.html">inbound</a></td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table></div>
        {% if obsoletion_projects %}
        <h3>Obsoletion and refactoring projects ({{ obsoletion_projects | length }})</h3>
        <p class="muted">Project pages tagged <code>OBSOLETION</code>.</p>
        <ul>
            {% for p in obsoletion_projects %}<li><a href="../projects/{{ p.slug }}.html">{{ p.title }}</a>{% if p.maturity %} <span class="muted">({{ p.maturity }})</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="panel" id="new-terms">
        <h2>Proposed new terms</h2>
        <p>{{ terms }} new-term proposals from {{ term_reviews }} gene and module reviews
            (top-level <code>proposed_new_terms</code>).
            <a href="proposed-new-terms.html">Browse proposals</a> &middot;
            <a href="proposed-new-terms.tsv">Download TSV</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" id="source-defects">
        <h2>Source defects</h2>
        <p class="muted">Errors found in another resource's records (a wrong gene product, a mis-keyed
            reference, a wrong evidence code), recorded as <code>source_defects</code> in gene and
            GO-CAM reviews. Each report lists the open defects for one resource.
            <a href="source-defects.tsv">Download TSV</a>.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
            <thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th class="num">Open</th><th class="num">Confirmed</th><th class="num">Probable</th><th class="num">Suspected</th><th class="num">All recorded</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
            {% for d in defects %}
            <tr><td><a href="source-defects/{{ d.resource }}.html">{{ d.resource }}</a></td>
                <td class="num">{{ d.open }}</td>
                <td class="num">{{ d.confidence.CONFIRMED }}</td>
                <td class="num">{{ d.confidence.PROBABLE }}</td>
                <td class="num">{{ d.confidence.SUSPECTED }}</td>
                <td class="num">{{ d.total }}</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table></div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" id="mappings">
        <h2>Mapping reviews</h2>
        <p class="muted">Reviews of the mappings from other vocabularies to GO that generate electronic
            annotations. See the <a href="../projects/{{ mapping_index }}.html">mapping reviews collection</a>.</p>
        <ul>
            {% for p in mapping_projects %}<li><a href="../projects/{{ p.slug }}.html">{{ p.title }}</a>{% if p.maturity %} <span class="muted">({{ p.maturity }})</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" id="rules">
        <h2>Rule reviews</h2>
        <p>{{ rule_reviews }} reviews of UniProt ARBA rules, with recommended changes.
            <a href="../rules/index.html">All rules</a> &middot; <a href="../../rules/arba/index.html">ARBA reviews</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
